<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-BHP says new bulk carrier delivered.</title>
<headline>RTRS-BHP says new bulk carrier delivered.</headline>
<dateline>MELBOURNE 1997-01-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Broken Hill Pty Co Ltd said on Thursday the bulk carrier &quot;Saraji Trader&quot; had been delivered to Green Ocean Bulk Shipping Ltd, a 50-50 joint venture between BHP Transport Pty Ltd and Kawasaki Kisen Kaisha Ltd.</p>
<p>The 169,900 dwt vessel built by Daewoo Heavy Industries Ltd was due to leave South Korea on Thursday and arrive in Hay Point, Queensland, on February 6 to load her first cargo, BHP said.</p>
<p>The &quot;Saraji Trader&quot; will carry coal and iron ore, and trade between ports in Europe, South America and Japan as well as the Australian ports of Port Hedland, Hay Point and Gladstone.</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
